{
 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the Kilo Code table. Kilo Code's CLI core is an OpenCode fork; at the original pins the published bus union at @kilocode/sdk@7.4.5 was byte-identical to @opencode-ai/sdk@1.17.18's (verified member by member in the design record) and the mapping carried the OpenCode table whole on Kilo's own identity. The SHIPPED runtime has since diverged from both the upstream and Kilo's own published npm types (verified against the 7.4.11 binary, which the published @kilocode/plugin + @kilocode/sdk 7.4.11 types lag): the hold-open permission.ask hook is gone, the ask/settle moments ride NEW bus types (permission.asked / permission.replied), and a followup-question surface exists (question.asked / question.replied). This fixture pins BOTH surfaces \u2014 the <=7.4.5 hook rows and the >=7.4.6 bus rows. Two moment shapes, both pinned at the adapter default posture (capture metadata; attention.* redacted): bus events from the plugin's `event` hook ({kind:'bus', event}) and the interception hooks (tool.execute.before/after, the hold-open permission.ask). Envelope identity (bus sessionID -> session; runs SYNTHESIZED per user-message/idle boundary \u2014 no turn id; callID pairing) and both permission control loops (the held hook; the >=7.4.6 reply-route delivery) are runtime state, pinned by the reference adapter smoke.",
 "identity": {
  "session_from": "properties.sessionID | properties.info.sessionID | properties.info.id | permission.sessionID | input.sessionID (per moment shape)",
  "run_from": null,
  "$comment": "No turn id is exposed; the adapter synthesizes one run per user-message/idle boundary (message.updated role:user opens unless a run is open \u2014 steering never double-opens; session.idle closes). callID pairs tool events exactly."
 },
