   "$comment": "a decision that settled outside the control loop (TUI-answered); the adapter suppresses this when its own loop already resolved the same vendor id \u2014 runtime state, smoke-pinned"
  },
  "permission_asked": {
   "input": {
    "kind": "bus",
    "event": {
     "type": "permission.asked",
     "properties": {
      "id": "perm_1",
      "type": "bash",
      "pattern": "rm *",
      "sessionID": "s_fix_1",
      "messageID": "msg_u1",
      "callID": "call_2",
      "title": "rm -rf build",
      "metadata": {},
      "time": {
       "created": 6
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "expected": {
    "type": "attention.requested",
    "data": {
     "kind": "permission",
     "prompt": "Permission requested: bash \u2014 rm -rf build",
     "options": [
      {
       "id": "once",
       "label": "Allow once"
      },
      {
       "id": "always",
       "label": "Always allow"
      },
      {
       "id": "reject",
       "label": "Reject"
      }
     ],
     "respond_via": [
      "control"
     ]
    },
    "subject": "bash"
   },
   "$comment": "the >=7.4.6 ask surface (verified against the shipped 7.4.11 binary): the hold-open hook is gone, the ask arrives as a bus NOTIFICATION while Kilo Code's own prompt runs in parallel, and the decision travels back over the server reply route (POST /session/{id}/permissions/{permissionID} {response, message?}) \u2014 options mirror that reply enum verbatim, and unmatched free text applies the refusing status WITH the guidance delivered as the reject message (new on this surface; the old hook's output carried status only)"
  },
  "question_asked": {
   "input": {
    "kind": "bus",
    "event": {
     "type": "question.asked",
     "properties": {
      "id": "que_1",
      "sessionID": "s_fix_1",
      "questions": [
       {
        "question": "Which database should the new service use?",
        "header": "Database",
        "options": [
         {
          "label": "PostgreSQL"
         },
         {
          "label": "SQLite"
         }
        ],
        "custom": true
       }
      ],
      "blocking": true,
      "tool": {
       "messageID": "msg_u1",
       "callID": "call_3"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "expected": {
    "type": "attention.requested",
    "data": {
     "kind": "form",
     "prompt": "kilocode asks 1 question",
     "fields": [
      {
       "id": "1",
       "type": "select",
       "label": "Database: Which database should the new service use?",
       "required": true,
       "other": true,
       "choices": [
        {
         "id": "1",
         "label": "PostgreSQL"
        },
        {
         "id": "2",
         "label": "SQLite"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "respond_via": [
      "control"
     ]
    },
    "subject": "que_1"
   },
   "$comment": "the >=7.4.6 followup-question surface: one bus ask -> ONE attention.requested(kind:\"form\") on the claude-code AskUserQuestion shape \u2014 index ids structural at any ceiling, labels gated at redacted+, `custom` (vendor default true) -> fields[].other; the adapter resolves choice ids back to the ORIGINAL vendor labels for delivery (POST /question/{requestID}/reply {answers: string[][]}), so redaction never rewrites what the vendor receives"
  },
  "question_replied": {
   "input": {
    "kind": "bus",
    "event": {
     "type": "question.replied",
     "properties": {
      "sessionID": "s_fix_1",
      "requestID": "que_1",
      "answers": [
       [
        "PostgreSQL"
       ]
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "expected": {
    "type": "attention.resolved",
    "data": {
     "resolution": "answered"
    },
    "subject": "que_1"
   },
   "$comment": "a question that settled on the vendor side (TUI answer) \u2014 the adapter suppresses this when its own control loop already delivered the reply, exactly the permission.replied dedupe rule"
  },
