 "sse_modes": {
  "$comment": "The Kilo Code SSE channel (the design record; the OTel-inbound mode discipline). For every bus moment above: companion (default \u2014 a plugin adapter may also observe and is the SOLE core-type authority) emits ONLY the channel-visible x.kilocode.* family, ZERO core types (core-mapped and adapter-suppressed moments carry as x.kilocode.<bus type> with empty data; already-vendor moments keep their mapped shape); primary (SSE-only deployments) emits the full bus mapping with the read-only-channel override: permission.updated -> attention.requested WITHOUT options or respond_via (nothing can answer through this channel \u2014 the REST actuator stays a design note), and todo.updated stays null (the receiver drives the same pinned diffTodos). Checked by run.js against the reference mode-policy module and by run.py as wire facts.",
